<article class="env-lemma" id="0AHD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AHD">Lemma <span data-tag="0AHD">74.8.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X \ar[rr]_ f \ar[rd]_ p &  &  Y \ar[dl]^ q \\  &  B }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a commutative diagram of morphisms of algebraic spaces over $S$. Assume that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is surjective, and syntomic (resp. smooth, resp. étale), 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$p$ is syntomic (resp. smooth, resp. étale). 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $q$ is syntomic (resp. smooth, resp. étale). </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We deduce this from the analogue for schemes. Namely, the problem is étale local on $B$ and $Y$ (Morphisms of Spaces, Lemmas <a href="/tag/03ZA" data-tag="03ZA">67.36.4</a>, <a href="/tag/03ZF" data-tag="03ZF">67.37.4</a>, and <a href="/tag/03XT" data-tag="03XT">67.39.2</a>). Hence we may assume that $B$ and $Y$ are affine schemes. Since $|X| \to |Y|$ is open (Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/042S" data-tag="042S">67.30.6</a>), we can choose an affine scheme $U$ and an étale morphism $U \to X$ such that the composition $U \to Y$ is surjective. In this case the result follows from Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/02KM" data-tag="02KM">35.14.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>